Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 48 CLINICAL DATA  Right core biopsy grade I infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DEFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO AN INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite angiolymphatic lymphatic invasion is seen  BREAST   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  SENTINEL   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL 13 LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 AUG 98 at 16 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tumor  is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 3cm fragment of oriented fibroadipose tissue inked in green and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm firm  tan white stellate mass present 1 1cm from the posterior margin  0 6cm from the anterior margin  and 0 7cm from the superior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  NOTE  The tumor mass is submitted enitirely in cassettes A through C  A  Tumor mass and posterior margin  B  Tumor mass and anterior margin  C  Tumor mass and superior margin  D  Representative sections of fibrofatty tissue surrounding tumor  E  Representative section of fatty breast tissue away from the lesion  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in three parts  Labeled  final shaved margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of small unremarkable fibrofatty fragments  submitted entirely in cassettes F I  Labeled  sentinel node   are two fatty fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE in aggregate  The larger fragment contains two lymph nodes  each sectioned and submitted separately in cassettes J and K  The smaller fatty fragment has  lymphoid tissue and is sectioned entirely in L  Labeled  RT axillary contents   are two fatty fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm in aggregate  with multiple unremarkable lymph nodes of up to 1 4cm  in cassettes M O  Gross Description by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   CARCINOMA PRESENT MARGINS NEGATIVE  O R  R